# Single env file — TEMPLATE.
#
# Copy this file to env/.env and fill in real values. Real env files are
# gitignored; only this *.example template is committed.
#
# This is the ONLY env file the scaffold reads. The previous two-layer
# layout (env/.env.{brand}.{environment} + env/.env.shared) was collapsed
# into one flat file so there is one source of truth for all environments
# and no per-developer file-sync to manage.
#
# Switching the active (brand, environment) pair:
#
#   The scaffold uses a single TARGET env var of the form
#   `<brand>-<environment>`. Defaults to `flighthub-staging2` (the team
#   does not have a dev environment, so staging2 is the standing default
#   for local runs).
#
#     TARGET=flighthub-staging1    npx playwright test --project=flighthub-chromium
#     TARGET=flighthub-staging2    npx playwright test --project=flighthub-chromium   # the default
#     TARGET=flighthub-staging3    npx playwright test --project=flighthub-chromium
#     TARGET=flighthub-prod        npx playwright test --project=flighthub-chromium
#     TARGET=justfly-staging1      npx playwright test --project=justfly-chromium
#     TARGET=justfly-staging2      npx playwright test --project=justfly-chromium     # the default
#     TARGET=justfly-staging3      npx playwright test --project=justfly-chromium
#     TARGET=justfly-prod          npx playwright test --project=justfly-chromium
#
#   Valid brands:        flighthub, justfly
#   Valid environments:  staging1, staging2, staging3, prod
#
#   `playwright.config.ts` parses TARGET, then for every key matching
#   `<BRAND>_<ENV>_<REST>` (uppercased) it sets `<BRAND>_<REST>` in
#   process.env. So `FLIGHTHUB_STAGING2_APP_URL` becomes
#   `FLIGHTHUB_APP_URL` when TARGET=flighthub-staging2 — the consumer
#   interface (`process.env.FLIGHTHUB_APP_URL` etc.) is unchanged.
#
#   The loader also exports `process.env.BRAND` and
#   `process.env.ENVIRONMENT` for any helper that branches on the active
#   brand at runtime (e.g. `helpers/shared/deactivateCustomer.ts`).
#
# Quick start:
#
#   1. cp env/.env.example env/.env
#   2. Fill in the URLs for at least one (brand, environment) pair you
#      will be running against — the staging2 pairs cover `npm test`.
#   3. Fill in the shared section (DB creds, APP_EMAIL / APP_PASSWORD,
#      RESPRO_*, Summit) — these are reused across every (brand, env).
#   4. Optionally fill in the per-brand seeded-booking values at the
#      bottom (BOOKING_*_FH / _JF) for the ref-search and portal-detail
#      happy-path specs under tests/shared/api/.
#
# scripts/db_access/*.py read the shared section directly via
# `set -a && source env/.env && set +a` (see scripts/db_access/README.md).

# ============================================================================
# Brand × Environment URL matrix
# ============================================================================
#
# Two URLs per (brand, environment) pair:
#   - <BRAND>_<ENV>_APP_URL  → frontend storefront URL (Playwright baseURL)
#   - <BRAND>_<ENV>_API_URL  → genesis Storefront API URL
#
# On every environment verified so far the storefront-api is served from
# the same origin as the app (e.g. GET https://staging2.flighthub.com/storefront-api/...
# returns 200; api.staging2.flighthub.com does not resolve). Other
# environments may need an `api.` subdomain — verify before filling in.
#
# Leave URLs blank for combos you do not run against — the loader only
# expands the active TARGET, so unused rows are inert.

# === Flighthub ===
FLIGHTHUB_STAGING1_APP_URL=
FLIGHTHUB_STAGING1_API_URL=

FLIGHTHUB_STAGING2_APP_URL=https://staging2.flighthub.com
FLIGHTHUB_STAGING2_API_URL=https://staging2.flighthub.com

FLIGHTHUB_STAGING3_APP_URL=
FLIGHTHUB_STAGING3_API_URL=

# WARNING: prod targets live production. Only run @smoke / @sanity /
# non-@destructive tests against prod. URLs verified live 2026-05.
FLIGHTHUB_PROD_APP_URL=https://www.flighthub.com
FLIGHTHUB_PROD_API_URL=https://www.flighthub.com

# === JustFly ===
JUSTFLY_STAGING1_APP_URL=
JUSTFLY_STAGING1_API_URL=

JUSTFLY_STAGING2_APP_URL=https://staging2.justfly.com
JUSTFLY_STAGING2_API_URL=https://staging2.justfly.com

JUSTFLY_STAGING3_APP_URL=
JUSTFLY_STAGING3_API_URL=

# WARNING: prod targets live production. Only run @smoke / @sanity /
# non-@destructive tests against prod.
JUSTFLY_PROD_APP_URL=https://www.justfly.com
JUSTFLY_PROD_API_URL=https://www.justfly.com

# Optional: utility / helper service URL (see config/util/util.ts).
# Uncomment and set when running suites that depend on it. Brand-prefix
# the key when it is genuinely brand-specific
# (FLIGHTHUB_STAGING2_UTILITY_URL=...); leave it unprefixed when the same
# host serves both brands.
# UTILITY_URL=

# ============================================================================
# Shared (cross-brand × cross-environment)
# ============================================================================
#
# Genuinely brand-agnostic values: shared genesis backend DB credentials,
# shared tooling credentials (Summit, Respro), and the shared genesis test
# customer account. Read straight from process.env.* by the same name.
#
# If a single key ever truly needs to differ per (brand, environment),
# define it brand-prefixed at the top of the file and have the consumer
# read the brand-prefixed copy — this loader does not synthesise per-
# (brand, env) overrides for unprefixed shared keys.

# === ClickHouse (analytics warehouse) ===
CLICKHOUSE_HOST=
CLICKHOUSE_PORT=8123
CLICKHOUSE_USER=
CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD=
CLICKHOUSE_DATABASE=default

# === MySQL (genesis operational database) ===
MYSQL_HOST=
MYSQL_PORT=3307
MYSQL_USER=
MYSQL_PASSWORD=
MYSQL_DATABASE=ota

# === MongoDB (genesis document store) ===
MONGODB_URI=
MONGODB_DATABASE=ota
# Optional safety allowlist for shared / multi-tenant deployments
# (see scripts/db_access/README.md and the db-access skill):
# MONGODB_ALLOWED_DATABASE=ota
# MONGODB_ALLOWED_COLLECTIONS=debug_logs,optimizer_logs

# === Summit (internal admin tool) ===
SUMMIT_USER=
SUMMIT_PASS=

# === Respro (internal reservations / fulfillment tool) ===
# Used by the cancelBookingViaRespro helper fixture for destructive-test
# cleanup. Single instance serves both brands.
RESPRO_URL=https://reservations.voyagesalacarte.ca
RESPRO_USER=
RESPRO_PASS=

# === Shared genesis test customer (auth-chain API specs) ===
# Used by the login-init / login-process / get-user-details / resend-totp
# happy-path tests under tests/shared/api/. Create the account once via
# POST /storefront-api/customer-sign-up against each brand's staging
# instance with the same email + password — the customer pool turned out
# to be per-brand on staging2 (see Trello card on the EPIC). A `+qa`
# plus-alias is recommended so TOTP / verification emails route to the
# main inbox without polluting it.
APP_EMAIL=
APP_PASSWORD=

# === Per-brand seeded bookings (ref-search / resend-totp / portal-detail specs) ===
# Each brand needs a real booking row in `ota.bookings` (`status: not_issued`
# is fine; `cancelled` is not — the ref-search handler hides cancelled
# bookings, though the `/service/portal/detail/{id_hash}` UI still renders
# them with a cancellation banner) plus the contact last name used at
# checkout and the row's `id_hash`. Genesis looks bookings up by `id +
# last_name + site_id`, so a Flighthub booking will not match the JustFly
# site_id filter and vice versa — both pairs are required for the
# cross-brand `tests/shared/api/refSearchInit.spec.ts`,
# `tests/shared/api/refSearchProcess.spec.ts`, and the booking-id branch
# of `tests/shared/api/resendTotp.spec.ts` happy paths.
#
# `BOOKING_ID_HASH_*` is the `bookings.id_hash` column — the opaque token
# the storefront uses for deep-links (`/service/portal/detail/{id_hash}`,
# `/service/portal/seat-request/{id_hash}`, etc). Used by the FlightHub
# booking-confirmation page object to navigate directly to a real booking
# without going through a destructive E2E checkout.
#
# Verify with:
#   set -a && source env/.env && set +a
#   python3 scripts/db_access/mysql_query.py query \
#     "SELECT id, id_hash, site_id, status, contact_last_name FROM bookings \
#      WHERE id IN (<BOOKING_ID_FH>, <BOOKING_ID_JF>)"
#
# Refresh cadence: TBD — bookings can be cancelled / refunded out of
# `not_issued` status, in which case the ref-search happy paths start
# failing with the `not-found` envelope. Tracked at
# https://trello.com/c/KKuEIcGg.
BOOKING_ID_FH=
BOOKING_ID_HASH_FH=
BOOKING_LAST_NAME_FH=
BOOKING_ID_JF=
BOOKING_ID_HASH_JF=
BOOKING_LAST_NAME_JF=
